# The Sun-3/80 PROM monitor commands `make sun3x` types (sim/mame/drive.py
# --cmds): one a line, typed at the monitor's prompt (`>`) or at an open
# location's (`?`), each followed by a carriage return. An empty line is a
# carriage return alone. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# The boot devices the PROM knows.
b ?
# Fill memory with a pattern, through the MMU (the PROM's map), long words.
f 100000 100100 a5a5a5a5 l
# ... and a byte-wide fill over part of it, which the long-word display must
# show merged.
f 100009 10000e 3c b
v 100000 100020 l
# Open a long word, step to the next, change it, step back over it, quit.
l 100004

5aa5c33c
q
v 100000 100010 b
# The PROM's first long words, its vectors, through its own mapping.
v fefe0000 fefe0040 l
# The function code the monitor's memory commands use.
s
